---
source: crates/lighthouse-report/tests/it/agent.rs
expression: "render_with(Format::Agent, &findings, &gap(), &briefing)"
---
design/coupling  warn  internal/jit/compile.go:350:1
  owner:       jit::compile#function
  message:     function coordinates 14 collaborators in its package
  requirement: Coupling SHOULD be judged from direct intra-package fan-in and fan-out, that is the functions and methods of the same package that call a symbol or are called by it, against deliberately high thresholds. Calls from other packages and from tests do not count: a widely used public function is a service, not a hub.
  context:     A dependency hub changes for many reasons. Rust: The unit is the Rust module (a `mod` and every inline module are distinct units). Methods count with their impl's type; calls through a receiver whose type is not written in the code are not seen, so fan counts are lower bounds.
  evidence:    callees=["a","b c"] fan_in=2 fan_out=14
  expected:    valid go example `ordinary-fan` (sample.go), canonical
                 package sample

                 func hub() {
                 	left()
                 	right()
                 }

                 func left()  {}
                 func right() {}

                 func a() { hub() }
                 func b() { hub() }
  fingerprint: 5da1c26cc609
  resolve:     lighthouse review resolve 5da1c26cc609 --verdict <verdict> --reason <reason> --reviewer-kind agent

design/private-helper-callers  info  src/lib.rs:7:1
  owner:       m::helper#function
  message:     private helper has one caller
  requirement: A private helper SHOULD have at least two callers.
  context:     A private helper with one caller is usually part of that caller. Go: A review item, not an error: a helper with one caller may be justified by naming a policy or isolating an abstraction level. Test callers do not count. Forwarding wrappers are reported by `design/no-single-use-wrapper`, and a function used as a value is not judged. Rust: Private free functions and methods that have exactly one caller outside test code and are never named as a value. A method that some call may reach through a receiver of unknown type is not judged.
  expected:    valid rust example `rust-valid` (src/lib.rs), canonical
                 pub fn run(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     clamp(x) + 1
                 }

                 pub fn other(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     clamp(x) + 2
                 }

                 fn clamp(x: u8) -> u8 {
                     if x > 10 { 10 } else { x }
                 }
  fingerprint: d3d6fba8ce7c
  resolve:     lighthouse review resolve d3d6fba8ce7c --verdict <verdict> --reason <reason> --reviewer-kind agent

acme/custom  error  a.txt:1:1
  message:     custom finding
  fingerprint: c8dfae349df1

